    74	
    75	At the fortieth minute Cael stopped charting the seal and started charting the gallery, and found that a third of it had stopped watching. Not from hostility. From the ordinary attrition of people who had come to see a case and were being read a list. The correspondents wrote nothing for nine minutes together. He entered it that night, and it was the coldest line the session produced: *the truth is admissible, unopposed, and boring. They have built a room in which our best work is a procedural delay.*
    76	
    77	Withrow's release of the response to the faculties had its own small scene, at the counter, because Bracken had objected — mildly, on procedure; a respondent's filing was the respondent's, and three registry-law faculties asking for it was three institutions about to have opinions. "Let them have opinions," Withrow said, signing the release. "The filing is perfect. Karis says so and Jent said so on the record. A perfect filing that nobody reads is a private loss. A perfect filing three faculties teach is a public fact, and public facts outlast rulings." She handed the copies to the courier. "I spent twenty years in the registry learning what survives a seat's discretion. Nothing survives it in the room. Everything survives it in the libraries."
    78	
