   187	
   188	"It's a man saying *not me*," said Brom.
   189	
   190	"It's a man saying *not in my name*." Karis folded her own sheet in half. "That's better. *Not me* is a feeling. *Not in my name* is on paper, under a signature, in a minute that will be kept for as long as the registry keeps anything." She stood up. "It's the only lever he had left. He pulled it as far as it would go."
   191	
   192	When the others had gone up, Cael stayed at the window with the copy, and read the third sentence over until the light went out of the glass.
