   145	"I did not tell you that I ran the inventories myself, both times, because the district was short-staffed and I was thorough." She sat down, which she did not do while he stood, and gestured him to the chair opposite, which she did not do either. "The second one I remember better, and I'll tell you it because you should hear a completed one from somebody who completed it, rather than assemble it out of Seln's grammar and your own imagination, which will be worse and will also be wrong in the wrong direction."
   146	
