/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md' in /Users/drive/fractured-path-monroe13
 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Chapter 20 — Lot Seventeen
     2	
     3	Three nights before the third sitting, the honest floor was the only floor on the hill where anybody was allowed to see what Cael was.
     4	
     5	They went in at the quarter to the eleventh bell, as they always did, on the key Rooke had lent Lira for the program's dawn drills and had told her he did not want to know about after dark. But the east hall was not what it had been. The shutters along the gallery had been closed since the Fourth-day by Rooke's order, and they did not need to be drawn. The chain still hung across the foot of the gallery stair with its padlock and its card, *CLOSED TO OBSERVERS*, so that Brom had to step over it to set the jug down on the bottom stair. The four lamps that the program now drilled under all day were standing at the corners of the painted crosses where the porters had left them, cold.
     6	
     7	"Well," said Lira, looking round the shut-up hall with her wrists half taped. "The whole floor's honest now. Nobody's allowed to watch any of it."
     8	
     9	Brom lit two of the lamps and left the other two dark, because two had always been the number. Karis sat on the gallery stair above the chain with her notebook open on her knee. Nobody had asked her to come. She had come anyway, every week since the first night, and counted.
    10	
    11	"What do you want?" said Cael.
    12	
    13	"The real one." Lira tore the last strip of tape with her teeth. "Everything you can't show in wing three. I've had six days of drilling under lamps, and I can't see my own heel coming any more, and I keep landing a quarter-beat late on things I could read in my sleep in daylight." She put her hands on her hips. "If I can see you coming at your true rate, in lamplight, I can see anybody coming at anything. So come."
    14	
    15	He looked at Brom. Brom looked at the lamps and then at him, and nodded once, which meant *I'm holding the room*.
    16	
